    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.10) and **Yordan Alvarez** (81.37). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an ideal matchup against Gusto; the combination of a favorable platoon advantage and a slow opposing delivery maximizes his stolen base potential, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains an auto-start despite a matchup against Pfaadt, as his elite .450 xwOBA and high-leverage spot in the two-hole make him nearly immune to the standard SP quality adjustments. **Trea Turner** (78.93) also projects as a premier play, as he exploits a soft matchup against P\u00e9rez to maintain his status as an elite speed-and-average contributor.\n\nWhile our starters are well-positioned, **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) represents the most significant platoon edge of the day, with his score bolstered by a favorable matchup against a struggling Ethan Pecko (6.19 xERA). Conversely, the most difficult decision involved **Junior Caminero** (55.11), who remains in the lineup despite facing deGrom; his talent floor keeps him ahead of **Chase Meidroth** (41.92), who was the most viable bench candidate but ultimately excluded due to a poor park factor and a low batting order position that limits his run-scoring opportunities. We are monitoring the status of **Josh Smith**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Yordan Alvarez** closely, as their scores are contingent on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; should they slide down the order, we have depth ready with **Casey Schmitt**, **Luis Pena**, or **Jacob Gonzalez** if needed. Note that **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Colt Keith** are unavailable today due to rest or injury, removing them from our daily cap calculations. We will monitor the weather closely, but as of now, the squad is cleared for a full push to gain ground in our chase for categories.",
